+## D2 formal kernels — mechanical extraction from nim-toml-serialization
+## Subject pin: 4aa8e2223649fc0837c490a4acfca7b8b1e756f9 (variant record: variant.patch;
+## this file is the ONLY delta from the baseline tree).
+##
+## Pragma shim: the external IR materializer reads the `{.axiom: [pre/post].}`
+## spec off the raw AST (src/infrastructure/external_ir_materializer.nim:273-298,
+## keyword expression form only). The counterexample-model replay compiles THIS
+## module with the real Nim compiler (src/verification/counterexample_replay.nim:499-504),
+## so the pragma must also be legal Nim: this user-pragma template mirrors Axiom's
+## own pattern (src/core/trusted/axiom_pragmas_macros.nim:11). An `untyped`
+## pragma argument is carried as syntax without semantic analysis, so the spec
+## payload is inert at compile time.
+template axiom*(val: untyped = "") {.pragma.}
+
+## Spec spelling note (2026-10-17): the byte-length law is spelled WITHOUT `if`
+## because the external-spec Canon frontend marks if-expressions lossy in pragma
+## context (toCanonKind lacks nkElifExpr/nkElseExpr; convertExprCanon lacks a
+## ckIfStmt arm — empirically established, see runs/defect.err of this slice).
+## On [0,255]: `1 + (code div 128)` is IDENTICAL to the piecewise law
+## (code < 128 -> 1; code >= 128 -> 2). S1 semantics unchanged, spelling only.
+
+## Defect kernel — extraction of scanHexEscape, lexer.nim:428-429
+## (`when T is string: res.add char(code)`): appending `char(code)` contributes
+## exactly ONE raw byte, for any code point.
+## Original lexer.nim sha256 @4aa8e22:
+## 19d69eed84f74c51fa1784b2e71a4525abc8d2b8aa854c567565d2d603133f4d
+func d2HexEscapeAppendLen*(code: int): int {.axiom: [
+    pre: (code >= 0 and code <= 255),
+    post: (result == (1 + (code div 128)))].} =
+  1
+
+## Control kernel — domain specialization ([0x00..0xFF], RFC 3629) of
+## scanUnicode, lexer.nim:413-414 (`res.add unicode.toUTF8(Rune(code))`):
+## the UTF-8 encoding of U+00HH occupies 1 byte below 0x80, 2 bytes from 0x80.
+## Body spelled with div/add for the same ingestion reason as the spec above.
+func d2Utf8AppendLen*(code: int): int {.axiom: [
+    pre: (code >= 0 and code <= 255),
+    post: (result == (1 + (code div 128)))].} =
+  1 + (code div 128)
